WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.315 --> 00:00:04.911
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.911 --> 00:00:08.740
I came to Stanford to
explore transformation.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.790
It is what matters most to me, and

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.851
as a world that has caused me
as much pain as it is pride.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.430
I'm not alone.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.460
Society is as obsessed with
transformation as I am.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:30.740
We're fascinated by the before and after,
who you were then and who you are now.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.570
On Instagram, it's the 10 year challenge.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.900
In nature,
it's the caterpillar turns butterfly.

00:00:44.402 --> 00:00:47.230
I spent my career in education
facilitating change.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.182
As a mixed race, Jewish woman,
I wanted to ensure that

00:00:54.182 --> 00:00:59.716
organizations changed to
embrace marginalized voices.

00:00:59.716 --> 00:01:04.299
So I worked for
organizations that create transformative

00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:09.642
experiences while they were
undergoing drastic internal change.

00:01:09.642 --> 00:01:13.322
Things like scaling local to national,

00:01:13.322 --> 00:01:18.634
transitioning CEOs,
infusing equity, and inclusion.

00:01:20.736 --> 00:01:23.660
I had a front row seat to
transformation of all kinds.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.897
It showed me that even the experts
still struggle to create and

00:01:30.897 --> 00:01:33.349
define transformation.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:37.160
And that's the thing.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.400
Do any of us really know what
transformation means when we say it?

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:46.340
Because if we want to change lives,
organizations, and

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.530
the worlds,
we need to start defining how we do it.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.342
I'm here to end the before and
after dichotomy.

00:01:56.342 --> 00:02:02.230
I want to shift us from seeing
transformation as an outcome to a process,

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:07.010
and there is no process more famous,

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:12.670
no transformation metaphor more cliched
than the caterpillar turns butterfly.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.870
I actually love this metaphor, and

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:22.575
as a former elementary school science
teacher, I'm very familiar with it.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.670
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; The caterpillar to butterfly

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.530
captures transformation's magic and
mystery.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:36.420
Yet, what happens inside
the chrysalis phase is unquestioned,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.620
unheard of, and untouched,
and that's the mistake.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.720
We should be talking about the chrysalis,
the true hero.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:54.432
The chrysalis holds the key to
how we can define transformation.

00:02:54.432 --> 00:02:59.049
So let's focus on the chrysalis
because what happens inside is

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:01.060
absolutely mind blowing.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.940
A caterpillar makes her
chrysalis from the inside out.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:15.944
To prepare, she anchors herself to a home,
usually a twig.

00:03:15.944 --> 00:03:20.024
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; She then bursts her head open to shed

00:03:20.024 --> 00:03:21.030
her skin.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.270
The underlying layer is the chrysalis.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:31.720
The chrysalis protects her and
camouflages with the outside worlds

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.970
with the hope that no one
notices what's about to happen.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.210
Inside the chrysalis,
she then actively breaks down,

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:48.490
she liquifies,
turning completely into mush.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:56.242
The only thing left are her
essential structures for breathing.

00:03:56.242 --> 00:03:59.940
Yet, even as mush,
she knows how to rebuild,

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:05.320
she builds each structure carefully,
her legs,

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.030
her wings, the patterns on her body.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:18.662
And when ready, she breaks free
until finally, she can fly.

00:04:25.643 --> 00:04:30.660
When caterpillars break down,
they know how

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:36.080
to create new,
better versions of themselves.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:45.520
They can even remember their time as a
caterpillar once they became a butterfly,

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:53.480
what they smelled,
what they liked, what scared them.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:02.873
At each step,
this transformation is active,

00:05:02.873 --> 00:05:08.470
messy, intentional, and personal.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.240
This is how we can define transformation.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.216
This is the magic.

00:05:14.922 --> 00:05:17.895
And I've learned this firsthand.

00:05:17.895 --> 00:05:20.680
I experienced a couple of
personal transformations.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:27.644
It took me years to
truly accept my identity

00:05:27.644 --> 00:05:32.165
as a black and white, Jewish woman.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:36.530
Yet, what truly taught me
the process of transformation,

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.860
to define it in real time was,

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.776
of all things, a bad break-up.

00:05:48.776 --> 00:05:53.040
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; A couple years ago, I was ending

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:58.250
a five-year relationship, starting a new
job, and learning to live in a new city.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.560
Feelings of finding myself were front and
center.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.040
I was angry.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:07.930
I was sad.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:11.580
And I was surrounded by people that
created transformation every day.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.160
How do you do that?

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.550
I never got that question answered,
which is why I'm here,

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:23.706
waxing nature metaphors and
divulging my story of liquifying.

00:06:23.706 --> 00:06:27.070
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; We need to talk about the breakdown.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:33.987
I went through the same
steps as that caterpillar.

00:06:33.987 --> 00:06:40.950
Step one, I anchored, the San Francisco
Bay Area, and later Stanford.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.060
Transformation often happens in these
immersive learning experiences because

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:49.438
you're rooted in a place to do the work.

00:06:51.358 --> 00:06:55.840
Step two, shed skin and form protection.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:02.430
I simultaneously switched jobs,
moved, ended a relationship, and

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:03.275
applied to business school.

00:07:03.275 --> 00:07:08.502
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; In many ways, my chrysalis has been

00:07:08.502 --> 00:07:13.953
my business school experience,
from application to today.

00:07:13.953 --> 00:07:19.627
Step three, break down.

00:07:19.627 --> 00:07:22.720
I definitely broke.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:26.781
I sat alone and slept alone.

00:07:26.781 --> 00:07:33.175
I cried every single day.

00:07:33.175 --> 00:07:35.599
I screamed.

00:07:35.599 --> 00:07:37.098
I don't scream.

00:07:37.098 --> 00:07:41.669
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I

00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:46.732
laid on my bedroom floor,
my version of mush.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.980
I was so lost.

00:07:53.287 --> 00:07:58.460
Step four,
Thoughtfully put yourself back together.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.705
I found me.

00:08:02.705 --> 00:08:09.950
I started writing again, after five years,
poetry mostly, and letters.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.640
I righted my wrongs and

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:17.450
accepted there were wrongs that
I would never be able to right.

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:23.770
I practiced presence,
balance, and gratitude.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:27.768
I actively, intentionally,
changed for the better.

00:08:30.217 --> 00:08:36.633
Step 5, break free, fly, and
remember where you came from.

00:08:38.272 --> 00:08:41.235
To be honest, I'm not here yet.

00:08:41.235 --> 00:08:44.730
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I'm in the messy, mushy middle.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.680
And I love being in my chrysalis.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:53.336
It gives me direction for
when to say yes and no.

00:08:53.336 --> 00:08:54.830
And for how to prepare for what's next.

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:01.830
That's the process, and we can all
prepare for what's next because it's so

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.280
much more than my transformation.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:07.660
It's why so many of us are at Stanford,
to search for

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:11.980
transformation ,to welcome it,
to facilitate it.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:19.120
Yet, we don't just come to Stanford
to be transformed, we do the work.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:25.852
We thoughtfully choose opportunities
that constitute our legs and wings,

00:09:25.852 --> 00:09:32.150
our careers, and organizations Maybe
we're all in the messy middle.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:38.330
At Stanford, and as a society, right now.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:44.980
We have the power and process to be better

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:51.180
because we can do more than change lives,
organizations, in the world.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.500
We can transform them.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.300
But it won't be enough
to repeat the words.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:04.274
We're going to have to
break them in ourselves,

00:10:04.274 --> 00:10:12.275
all the way down, in order to build
back up into something beautiful.

00:10:12.275 --> 00:10:13.479
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE].

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:18.068
[MUSIC]

